        "## DATA UNDERSTANDING\n",
        "\n",
        "Here is a breakdown of what each variable in the datasets means. This helps clarify what kind of information we’re working with, from movie titles and release dates to revenues, ratings, genres, and more. Each dataset contributes a unique lens through which we can explore film trends and patterns:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **The Numbers**: Focuses on financials—production budgets and grosses, giving insight into economic viability.\n",
        "* **Box Office Mojo**: Emphasizes domestic vs. international earnings, with added context from studio information.\n",
        "* **TMDb**: Offers popularity metrics, genre IDs, and voting data sourced from a broad user base.\n",
        "* **Rotten Tomatoes**: Brings in critic reviews, freshness ratings, and maturity classifications, helping us evaluate critical reception.\n",
        "* **IMDb**: Provides user-driven ratings, runtime, and genre tags—ideal for understanding audience sentiment and content classification.\n",
        "\n",
        "Each variable listed under these datasets defines a dimension we can explore.\n",
        "\n",
